{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328691Z","id":"0c0ad1bbb7f45b2607fba2bf5b2861ddbf2d38e90e03d8dcc69dc19893ee3950","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:integration_bundle, :integration_full_loop and :integration_locked_daemon each launch the debug app in the logged-in session (its window opens on the desktop) and take from 6 s to about 3 minutes (full_loop waits past the shell's 30 s hidden threshold twice). AGENTS.md asks the whole check suite to stay under two minutes on a warm cache and checks to need no display, and the native gates never ran them either (just app-integration-native). So they are manual and exclusive; just app-integration runs them. Running them in just ci would need a decision: accept the time and the windows on the owner's Mac, or run them only where a macOS runner with a session exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":439},"content_hash":"d702364c9de85bde34d3a4a1582ad4ef4bd0edbdf2adea6dd5034172fcc22776"},"summary":"The macOS integration tests are Bazel tests but tagged manual, so just ci does not run them","tags":["status:needs-decision","integration","ci","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328836Z","id":"bc952edafa3cd490211c762145aff5e44226cb83bbb4b2df62f1ab3205f99d56","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:apk matches Gradle's APK on package, versionCode, versionName, SDK levels, permissions, launcher activity (dev.empathic.clax_app.MainActivity), ABIs, extractNativeLibs, native libraries and signing certificate (:apk_test, and aapt2 dump badging diffed against flutter build apk's), and //apps/clax_app:macos_app matches flutter build macos's bundle ID, version, frameworks, entitlements and helper signature (:macos_app_test); the macOS integration tests ran the debug app (integration_locked_daemon and integration_bundle passed). Not done: installing the APK on a phone (scripts/app-phone.sh was only dry-run) and launching the release macOS app, which shares the installed app's bundle ID and so its sandbox container.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":251},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"9ac1175065c4040a930ccf0e63558438f8df5ae4db537606de073c6ed6b6e777"},"suggested_fix":"just app-phone on the owner's phone, then open an app, a WebView, notifications and dictation; and open the zip's clax_app.app on a Mac whose Clax data may be touched.","summary":"Neither the Bazel-built APK nor the Bazel-built macOS app was run on a device","tags":["unverified","apk","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/pubspec.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086068Z","id":"1568785228d6f2c63039a35fc132da77face87ac74ac1b9b23ca7ae5efe7d4e2","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). cryptography is used for bundle signing and hashing: Ed25519 keys and signatures (lib/platform/bundle_key.dart, lib/bundle/signing.dart) and SHA-256 (lib/bundle/content_hash.dart). Its LICENSE (pub cache, rules_flutter++flutter+clax_app_pub__cryptography/LICENSE) is the Apache License 2.0 alone. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) replace it: SHA-256 from package:crypto (BSD-3-Clause, already in pubspec.lock as a transitive dependency) and Ed25519 from a BSD- or MIT-licensed Dart package, its license to be checked; (c) do the signing in the embedded clax or the platform (Android Keystore, CryptoKit) over a channel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":11},"content_hash":"783efdecc10a1abbd005bb8729f00ab77d2f27eec74b5acb95c0cdf8727a9198"},"summary":"The app ships cryptography 2.9.0, which is Apache-2.0 only, under GPL-2.0-only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/pubspec.yaml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086268Z","id":"b530c07f74e3c38b3a8374a41551c36260a659a693c58d1cf4ef5d86c18960d2","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). flutter_timezone gives the device's time zone name (lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart). Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) replace it with a method on the app's own platform channel (TimeZone.getDefault().id in android/app/src/main/kotlin, TimeZone.current.identifier in the macOS runner), a few lines each.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"d0e3ce6f5cd2cb648e34079cbc4fb161f49642c6aa7bd0ad81b1c97cccf9b14e"},"summary":"The app ships flutter_timezone 5.1.1, which is Apache-2.0 only, under GPL-2.0-only","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/pubspec.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086465Z","id":"330514d7ea99ba9c6a1f321fc37595e67ee467f2e87923219d4fb905b2151128","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). image_picker (pubspec.yaml:20) picks photos for apps' camera and photo capabilities; its Android implementation's LICENSE is BSD-3-Clause for the plugin plus the Apache License 2.0 for the aFileChooser code it includes. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries; (b) pick images through file_picker (MIT, already a dependency, pubspec.yaml:12) or Android's photo picker intent on the app's own channel, and drop image_picker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"bb7c29f2d4a13da94c976901e72e7a21616b0681d0ed0d062e36eba0a249bd30"},"summary":"image_picker_android 0.8.13+25 bundles aFileChooser, Apache-2.0 only, in the GPL-2.0-only app","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/pubspec.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086632Z","id":"066b08ce1c7bf2ac5c4763d15ee6bf79d5507f17ed6977803de2aea1b7f4c27a","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). clock (a Dart team package) is a dependency of package_info_plus, speech_to_text and flutter_local_notifications, not of the app's own code. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries (the practical one: replacing it means replacing all three plugins); (b) replace those three plugins.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"801a10b0b5d1e4075b7198410dc2dac7d9a60ef945fc47274ef016a53eb68288"},"summary":"The app ships clock 1.1.3, Apache-2.0 only, through package_info_plus, speech_to_text and flutter_local_notifications","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/pubspec.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.086741Z","id":"5eb75b018951d70067f9b61f9a4d1c48a52adaaedd58e78095fe21a33e11fd3d","body":{"detail":"Apache-2.0-only code is incompatible with GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE lists apps/clax_app under GPL-2.0-only). material_color_utilities is a dependency of the Flutter framework itself (package:flutter's Material library), so every build of the app links it. GPLv2's system-library exception does not fit: it is bundled in the APK and the macOS app, not part of the operating system. Options: (a) an additional permission in apps/clax_app/LICENSE and LICENSE (Empathic, Inc. holds the copyright and the CLA covers contributions) letting the app be distributed with Apache-2.0 libraries (the only practical one; the Flutter engine, libflutter.so, also bundles third-party code under several licenses that this audit did not enumerate); (b) none short of leaving Material.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":618},"end":{"line":625},"content_hash":"e896b45a6f477469104cfa24d1db550a3eee8fad014142c2a7aed2a58684ee73"},"summary":"Every Material Flutter build ships material_color_utilities 0.13.0, Apache-2.0 only, in the GPL-2.0-only app","tags":["license","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:02:17.087322Z","id":"3a6374be5eafc38a9ceb54231da5604aeb527c986bc9d41f80cdd989c9003388","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter's flutter_application writes NOTICES.Z only from its license_files attribute, which :app does not set; `unzip -p bazel-bin/apps/clax_app/apk.apk assets/flutter_assets/NOTICES.Z` is 20 bytes of gzip with no text. A `flutter build` gathers every pub package's LICENSE and the engine's into it. The MIT and BSD licenses of most of the app's Dart packages (pubspec.lock) and of the Flutter engine require their notices in a binary distribution, which showLicensePage (lib/ui/licences.dart) would show. Clax's own notice is registered separately (registerClaxLicence) and does show. Fix: pass the pub packages' LICENSE files and the engine's LICENSE as license_files, in the format LicenseRegistry parses (package names, a blank line, the text, entries split by a line of 80 dashes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"2d8831a7e2197e709320b1fe12cde868f48dbc54a8c307c353c3fd9f5cf341bc"},"summary":"The Bazel-built app's licences page lists no third-party licences: NOTICES.Z in the APK is empty","tags":["license","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:26:27.057875Z","id":"761385c25da8d23e316a3723264a896858f4e6ad75de458e032d20687c1e896c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: :app bundles //apps/clax_app:notices as license_files. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:apk_test //apps/clax_app:macos_app_test passes with 'PASS: NOTICES holds the third-party notices (1859246 bytes)' (APK) and (1861847 bytes) (macOS), and NOTICES names webview_flutter, archive, flutter, skia, ring, tokio and rusqlite; //apps/clax_app:ui_licences_test passes, the licences page listing webview_flutter.","supersedes":"3a6374be5eafc38a9ceb54231da5604aeb527c986bc9d41f80cdd989c9003388","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:34.315357Z","id":"97e118c3bf2d9500f87ce00073bedcf84d41b8d9ece5249bf4c8c0711932e2b8","body":{"detail":"Strings the person can read that live outside copy_sources keep straight apostrophes or raw error text: the agent's failure reasons in thread replies (\"its data couldn't be updated\", apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:689 and apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:1691; \"couldn't be undone: ${e.message}\", finish.dart:698), the update and install refusals' details (['$e'] in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:248,362 and apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:238), and \"This app cannot be shared: ${e.message}.\" (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/exporter.dart:240). `python3 scripts/check-copy.py $(git ls-files 'apps/clax_app/lib/**.dart')` lists about 125 more findings, most of them prompt and tool text the model reads (lib/agent/prompt.dart, lib/agent/tools/*.dart), which keep straight quotes. \"Couldn't reach the Claude API\" (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:422) is also matched by text in lib/platform/network_pause.dart and its tests, so it changes together with them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":309},"content_hash":"0769208fec5c09610d46f8131c76370977bac93978b5c19b983fe22a2321d388"},"suggested_fix":"Curl the reply and refusal texts above (matching stored replies both ways, as failure.dart's _spentWords does), show their details through userMessage, then add lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, lib/agent/loop.dart and lib/bundle/*.dart to copy_sources with `// copy-check: allow` on model-facing lines.","summary":"//scripts:check_copy reads only lib/ui, lib/home, lib/app.dart, lib/agent/failure.dart, home/*.js and the kit: user-visible text elsewhere in lib/ is unchecked","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:26:18.953456Z","id":"fb3a727a85f37d5e651f20c829ce618781e830e7fdaf8307ea464fa8e38c0541","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:ios_app bundles the same NOTICES as the other platforms (flutter_application :app, license_files = [\":notices\"]), whose rust_binaries are //crates/clax-cli's Android and macOS binaries. On iOS the daemon is //crates/clax-ios:clax_ios_c, linked into the Runner, and its dependency tree (crates/clax-ios/Cargo.toml) is not what :notices walks. The sets likely coincide today, since both reach clax-server and its dependencies, but nothing checks it: a crate only clax-ios links would ship on iOS without its notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":432},"content_hash":"5e09fe3a63bc524f804640e5911773d6d8dd52e1fa27369c69ba68d69accfb42"},"suggested_fix":"Add the clax-ios static library to rust_binaries once bazel/flutter/notices.bzl's RustLicensesInfo aspect can walk it, or check that its crate set is a subset of clax_opt's.","summary":"The iOS app's NOTICES lists the Rust crates of clax-cli's binaries, not of crates/clax-ios","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.491913Z","id":"e9f1ca66c2b295f37bb0ffb28ac91369a18d4124a16ea7752a831b7555b8b954","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:apk matches Gradle's APK on package, versionCode, versionName, SDK levels, permissions, launcher activity (dev.empathic.clax_app.MainActivity), ABIs, extractNativeLibs, native libraries and signing certificate (:apk_test, and aapt2 dump badging diffed against flutter build apk's), and //apps/clax_app:macos_app matches flutter build macos's bundle ID, version, frameworks, entitlements and helper signature (:macos_app_test); the macOS integration tests ran the debug app (integration_locked_daemon and integration_bundle passed). Not done: installing the APK on a phone (scripts/app-phone.sh was only dry-run) and launching the release macOS app, which shares the installed app's bundle ID and so its sandbox container.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":500},"end":{"line":523},"content_hash":"265fee7ce70b6b515da06397bbe33e8f708f840a0988e3295df7bb0b345ac58d"},"suggested_fix":"just app-phone on the owner's phone, then open an app, a WebView, notifications and dictation; and open the zip's clax_app.app on a Mac whose Clax data may be touched.","summary":"Neither the Bazel-built APK nor the Bazel-built macOS app was run on a device","supersedes":"bc952edafa3cd490211c762145aff5e44226cb83bbb4b2df62f1ab3205f99d56","tags":["unverified","apk","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.596158Z","id":"cb063072d4932f5eda02217c7871360354ba83508fc0fb43a5a24d3295294e53","body":{"detail":"Strings the person can read that live outside copy_sources keep straight apostrophes or raw error text: the agent's failure reasons in thread replies (\"its data couldn't be updated\", apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:689 and apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:1691; \"couldn't be undone: ${e.message}\", finish.dart:698), the update and install refusals' details (['$e'] in apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart:248,362 and apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart:238), and \"This app cannot be shared: ${e.message}.\" (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/exporter.dart:240). `python3 scripts/check-copy.py $(git ls-files 'apps/clax_app/lib/**.dart')` lists about 125 more findings, most of them prompt and tool text the model reads (lib/agent/prompt.dart, lib/agent/tools/*.dart), which keep straight quotes. \"Couldn't reach the Claude API\" (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:422) is also matched by text in lib/platform/network_pause.dart and its tests, so it changes together with them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":309},"content_hash":"a0184e08aecfb30dacaeb2a0f454f1722884da032a1c12b9f15574e15b90986e"},"suggested_fix":"Curl the reply and refusal texts above (matching stored replies both ways, as failure.dart's _spentWords does), show their details through userMessage, then add lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, lib/agent/loop.dart and lib/bundle/*.dart to copy_sources with `// copy-check: allow` on model-facing lines.","summary":"//scripts:check_copy reads only lib/ui, lib/home, lib/app.dart, lib/agent/failure.dart, home/*.js and the kit: user-visible text elsewhere in lib/ is unchecked","supersedes":"97e118c3bf2d9500f87ce00073bedcf84d41b8d9ece5249bf4c8c0711932e2b8","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.689901Z","id":"489c9160fb6a2221d9447dabd0308fb38ac972864f1f674a5750bc90a1087cd3","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:integration_bundle, :integration_full_loop and :integration_locked_daemon each launch the debug app in the logged-in session (its window opens on the desktop) and take from 6 s to about 3 minutes (full_loop waits past the shell's 30 s hidden threshold twice). AGENTS.md asks the whole check suite to stay under two minutes on a warm cache and checks to need no display, and the native gates never ran them either (just app-integration-native). So they are manual and exclusive; just app-integration runs them. Running them in just ci would need a decision: accept the time and the windows on the owner's Mac, or run them only where a macOS runner with a session exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":845},"end":{"line":851},"content_hash":"ca2a5ea1a7900ef9af29681c8d1e8852eccd702d524bf08943a988728f4cdc62"},"summary":"The macOS integration tests are Bazel tests but tagged manual, so just ci does not run them","supersedes":"0c0ad1bbb7f45b2607fba2bf5b2861ddbf2d38e90e03d8dcc69dc19893ee3950","tags":["status:needs-decision","integration","ci","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
