ession:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:59:51.746312Z","id":"39aa666e11b66e6232d4e076267cde8a20a218aef1306ede416ce41cfaac549f","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:ios_app bundles the same NOTICES as the other platforms (flutter_application :app, license_files = [\":notices\"]), whose rust_binaries are //crates/clax-cli's Android and macOS binaries. On iOS the daemon is //crates/clax-ios:clax_ios_c, linked into the Runner, and its dependency tree (crates/clax-ios/Cargo.toml) is not what :notices walks. The sets likely coincide today, since both reach clax-server and its dependencies, but nothing checks it: a crate only clax-ios links would ship on iOS without its notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":430},"end":{"line":434},"content_hash":"5e09fe3a63bc524f804640e5911773d6d8dd52e1fa27369c69ba68d69accfb42"},"suggested_fix":"Add the clax-ios static library to rust_binaries once bazel/flutter/notices.bzl's RustLicensesInfo aspect can walk it, or check that its crate set is a subset of clax_opt's.","summary":"The iOS app's NOTICES lists the Rust crates of clax-cli's binaries, not of crates/clax-ios","supersedes":"fb3a727a85f37d5e651f20c829ce618781e830e7fdaf8307ea464fa8e38c0541","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:59:51.799131Z","id":"d2b4ea82281a877f1882203306428997e5c00e021c35208be8e4d72cf30da2e2","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:apk matches Gradle's APK on package, versionCode, versionName, SDK levels, permissions, launcher activity (dev.empathic.clax_app.MainActivity), ABIs, extractNativeLibs, native libraries and signing certificate (:apk_test, and aapt2 dump badging diffed against flutter build apk's), and //apps/clax_app:macos_app matches flutter build macos's bundle ID, version, frameworks, entitlements and helper signature (:macos_app_test); the macOS integration tests ran the debug app (integration_locked_daemon and integration_bundle passed). Not done: installing the APK on a phone (scripts/app-phone.sh was only dry-run) and launching the release macOS app, which shares the installed app's bundle ID and so its sandbox container.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":502},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"265fee7ce70b6b515da06397bbe33e8f708f840a0988e3295df7bb0b345ac58d"},"suggested_fix":"just app-phone on the owner's phone, then open an app, a WebView, notifications and dictation; and open the zip's clax_app.app on a Mac whose Clax data may be touched.","summary":"Neither the Bazel-built APK nor the Bazel-built macOS app was run on a device","supersedes":"e9f1ca66c2b295f37bb0ffb28ac91369a18d4124a16ea7752a831b7555b8b954","tags":["unverified","apk","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:59:51.851580Z","id":"46900270281db7802a6a3e0df6b5c53d0b7397cb4a4188f78c681c70c17e88c8","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:integration_bundle, :integration_full_loop and :integration_locked_daemon each launch the debug app in the logged-in session (its window opens on the desktop) and take from 6 s to about 3 minutes (full_loop waits past the shell's 30 s hidden threshold twice). AGENTS.md asks the whole check suite to stay under two minutes on a warm cache and checks to need no display, and the native gates never ran them either (just app-integration-native). So they are manual and exclusive; just app-integration runs them. Running them in just ci would need a decision: accept the time and the windows on the owner's Mac, or run them only where a macOS runner with a session exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":847},"end":{"line":853},"content_hash":"ca2a5ea1a7900ef9af29681c8d1e8852eccd702d524bf08943a988728f4cdc62"},"summary":"The macOS integration tests are Bazel tests but tagged manual, so just ci does not run them","supersedes":"489c9160fb6a2221d9447dabd0308fb38ac972864f1f674a5750bc90a1087cd3","tags":["status:needs-decision","integration","ci","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:08:39.935398Z","id":"52f4b2890ca90cec5c76126d6490327aa8c53342b574e3f85866961e45619cd9","body":{"detail":"lib/'s 18 folders form one import cycle (python3 bazel/flutter/dart_graph.py apps/clax_app --report lists it): among others lib/core imports lib/clax (core_transport.dart), lib/clax imports lib/agent (fake_api.dart) and lib/daemon (transport.dart), lib/daemon imports lib/platform (daemon_key.dart), lib/platform imports lib/agent (network_pause.dart, timings.dart), lib/agent imports lib/ui (ai_consent.dart, failure.dart), and lib/ui imports lib/version.dart. Bazel targets cannot form a cycle, so per-folder libraries would be one library for all of lib/ and select every test. At file grain only eight small cycles remain, each one target.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"82da019020c6f07ff83cb5f5a871b89bcc1b8faa69b0b2f961e3e0b46b3a2ed7"},"summary":"A library per folder of lib/ instead of one per Dart library","tags":["revisit:dart_graph.py --report shows lib/'s folders without a cycle","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:08:39.935869Z","id":"fe76dc43b9175685fb55f3b0a71439e178a2c845d5ace1107974f65c3a1d71d7","body":{"detail":"TEST_DATA (assets/**, home/**, test/fixtures/**, the core's icon fixtures, the store's job moves, //web:contract_files) is the data of all suites. A file read by one test (test/fixtures/relay_answer_parts.json, the job moves fixture) selects all 216.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"ff205e4d767a7dbddc3c791ef26f117c9800c86abaaae8e90b0bdea206ee7094"},"summary":"Every suite carries TEST_DATA, so a change to any asset, fixture or contract file selects every unit test","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:08:39.936193Z","id":"25d18e77b9e031c14b1743c49174a459c28eddc338373c6d3b369b3b77a7fc9e","body":{"detail":"The check moved out of flutter_notices (bazel/flutter/notices.bzl) so NOTICES does not depend on the app's Dart. `bazel test //...` and scripts/affected-tests.sh run it (it depends on :clax_app); `bazel build //apps/clax_app:apk` alone now ships a NOTICES whose pub list may be stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":451},"content_hash":"3a31ca5eded4e2073a7d69bebe8def10cec8cbe04c6e47b9e8ccc056853acdab"},"summary":"A pub package the app gains or loses fails :notices_pub_test, no longer a build of the APK or the macOS app","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:17:18.004947Z","id":"edf6272597dd4d0f88f987bffbf57088534f87ae1a01432ba045fee4366e7a4f","body":{"detail":"They are out of every app (macos_app and the integration apps, the iOS runner and its integration apps, the APK's native_files). They still build under //... (and :macos_clax signs clax_opt). They go with the daemon code, crates/clax-ios, ios/Daemon/ClaxDaemon.swift and macos/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":637},"end":{"line":647},"content_hash":"46de045b9b4f8729e40752599983d5c8db3875c92a9d64790cb8afbe67c6b4ea"},"summary":"The earlier daemon's ship targets stay defined though no app uses them: :macos_clax (with //crates/clax-cli:clax_opt), bazel/flutter/ios.bzl's ios_daemon over crates/clax-ios, and bazel/android/clax.bzl","tags":["core","cleanup","revisit:the daemon Dart code and crates/clax-ios are deleted","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:53.930501Z","id":"4c643efb4ab09ece4b8043344881d422a39de21306323cd828b779d0a812add1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The earlier daemon's ship targets are deleted: :macos_clax and macos_helper (bazel/flutter/macos.bzl), ios_daemon (bazel/flutter/ios.bzl) with crates/clax-ios and ios/Daemon/ClaxDaemon.swift, bazel/android/clax.bzl with //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_{arm64,x86_64}, and macos/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements. bazelisk query //... loads clean (exit 0), and git grep -e macos_clax -e ios_daemon -e clax_android_arm -e ClaxDaemon -- apps scripts bazel crates justfile finds them only in .qual files; //apps/clax_app:apk_test, :macos_app_test and :ios_app_test pass.","supersedes":"edf6272597dd4d0f88f987bffbf57088534f87ae1a01432ba045fee4366e7a4f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.052147Z","id":"6c7da58dcf4d970ed1eeec09ff2b35c2f297fbf6d8347cb369320e09bdb8b78c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed by f1c07f346b12: :notices' rust_binaries are //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_android_arm64, :clax_embed_android_x86_64 and :clax_embed_shared in the app's configuration, the same crates as clax_embed_ios_c (apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel flutter_notices), and crates/clax-ios is deleted in f1c07f346b12. //apps/clax_app:ios_app_test passes.","supersedes":"39aa666e11b66e6232d4e076267cde8a20a218aef1306ede416ce41cfaac549f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
